// tap-echo: --buffer 65535
// RFC 5961 3.2 / Linux: an in-window RST away from RCV.NXT in SYN-RECEIVED gets a
// challenge ACK and the half-open connection survives, same as the other synchronized
// states (scripts/freebsd-rcv-rst-*-right-edge-secure.pkt). Linux's tcp_rcv_state_process
// runs tcp_validate_incoming (tcp_input.c:5945-6032, called unconditionally before its
// per-state switch, e.g. tcp_input.c:6801) for a SYN_RECV full socket the same as any
// other state: an RST resets only at tp->rcv_nxt (or tcp_reset_check's RCV.NXT-1-after-FIN
// case, or the SACK right edge); anything else in-window draws tcp_send_challenge_ack and
// is discarded. Zhida's socket/tcp.rs process() now includes State::SynReceived in the
// same exact-match-or-challenge-ACK RST block the other six synchronized states use
// (tcp.rs:1883-1922); the exact-match branch resets a SYN-RECEIVED socket that came from
// LISTEN back to LISTEN (tcp.rs:1910-1918), matching upstream's own
// freebsd-rcv-rst-syn-rcvd-via-listen-left-edge-secure.pkt, which already asserts that for
// an RST at RCV.NXT.
// Ensure that the reception of a TCP RST with SEG.SEQ = RCV.NXT + RCV.WND - 1
// in the SYN-RCVD state triggers the sending of a challenge ACK.
// Adapted from freebsd-net/tcp-testsuite commit 04b8c73fc5081fe3792f1bed9168c9b22aaedddb,
// state-event-engine/rcv-rst-syn-rcvd/rcv-rst-syn-rcvd-via-listen-right-edge-secure-ipv4.pkt
// (BSD-2-Clause; notice below). Changes for Zhida's packet-only runner, tap-echo
// being the application (fuzz/packetdrill/README.md, "Upstream suites"):
// - IPv4 variant. Dropped: sysctls, which set FreeBSD defaults and
//   net.inet.tcp.insecure_rst=0 (RFC 5961 RST checks on); Zhida has no such switch;
//   fcntl; getsockopt(SO_RCVBUF); --tolerance_usecs=75000 (the runner keeps
//   packetdrill's 4 ms); sockstat and tcpdrop commands except where replaced below.
// - socket/bind/listen dropped: tap-echo listens on port 8080.
// - Receive window: tap-echo --buffer 65535, so Zhida's RCV.WND is 65535, its
//   advertised window (no window scale), as upstream's.
//
